Write a program that takes a string and displays the first a character it encounters, followed by a newline.
If there is no a in the string, the program simply displays a newline.
If the number of parameters is not 1, the program displays a followed by a newline.
Examples:
./aff_a "abc"
a

./aff_a "bonjour"
# only newline

./aff_a "abc" "def"
a

Allowd function: write
***************************
write(1, "z\n", 2);
write(1, "a\n", 2);
